    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76cc9065_9c2030ac",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/BufferManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-19T23:15:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That make sense. I imagine this will change back to a pointer to the DBM once we decouple the reuse pool from the BufferInfo, though I like your suggestions as an intermediate state.\n\n---\nP.S.: I was halfway through implementing this but then the mutual dependency between DrawBufferManager and ScratchBuffer got in the way: `DrawBufferManager::getScratchBuffer` returns a `ScratchBuffer` by value so `ScratchBuffer` needs to be declared before DBM. `DrawBufferManager::BufferInfo` is a nested class so it can\u0027t be forward declared.\n\nI could change `getScratchBuffer` to return a `std::unique_ptr\u003cScratchBuffer\u003e` which would resolve the issue but I wanted to avoid the heap allocation as I intended `ScratchBuffer` to be a mostly lightweight move-only type and ScratchBuffers will be allocated frequently.",
      "parentUuid": "c4ad4380_aa409bd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "966c34243b4eeafcbe8c8d9aed1689fa87c01ec7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
