      "writtenOn": "2024-03-20T14:04:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think keeping it as a value type makes the most sense, so I\u0027m glad you found a solution. One approach we could do is split `BufferInfo` into two pieces: the \"type\" configuration such as alignment and usage that is immutable and needs to be shared with the ScratchBuffer; and the current buffer tracking used for the non-scratch suballocations. The configuration could be a public struct defined outside of DBM.",
